Description: [Installutil.exe](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/InstallUtil) is a Windows utility that allows developers to install and uninstall .NET applications. It can be used to execute arbitrary code on the system.

## How it works

### Code execution

#### Method 1: Execute code from a DLL

The following example demonstrates how to execute code from a DLL using `InstallUtil.exe`. The DLL contains a method named `Main` that will be executed when the DLL is loaded.

```csharp
using System;
using System.IO;
using System.Reflection;

class Program
{
    static void Main(string[] args)
    {
        Console.WriteLine("Hello, world!");
    }
}

Assembly assembly = Assembly.LoadFile(@"C:\path\to\your\assembly.dll");
```

